This code provides a complete solution for controlling a submersible 12V water pump using a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B, with the pigpio library for GPIO control and the wiringPi library for SPI communication. It reads moisture data from a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC, and activates the pump based on configurable thresholds and durations. The program logs all actions and handles errors gracefully, ensuring a clean shutdown on exit.

