This code provides a basic framework for a Theremin-like instrument using a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It reads distance from an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor and maps it to an audio frequency, and reads a photoresistor value via an MCP3008 ADC to control volume. It handles errors gracefully, manages resources cleanly on SIGINT, and saves and loads calibration data. Note that the PWM duty cycle control for volume is not implemented in this code snippet.

