This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to interface with a VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor using the pigpio library. It triggers a distance reading on the rising edge of GPIO24 using an interrupt service routine (ISR). Based on the measured distance, it controls a small DC motor via GPIO17 (forward) and GPIO18 (backward). The program handles errors, retries failed I2C transactions with exponential backoff, and stops the motor safely if the sensor is absent or a bus error occurs. It logs distance readings and motor state changes to the console and ensures clean resource release on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

