This code initializes the pigpio library, opens the I2C bus, and sets up a signal handler for graceful shutdown. It repeatedly sends a command to the STS30-DIS sensor to perform a high-repeatability measurement, waits for the conversion, reads the data, and validates the CRC-8 checksum. The temperature is then calculated and logged with an ISO-8601 timestamp. Errors during I2C communication or CRC mismatches are logged to a separate file. The program handles SIGINT to ensure resources are released cleanly on exit.

