This code provides a complete, compilable C program for interfacing with an ADXL345 accelerometer over I2C on a Raspberry Pi 5. It reads the X, Y, and Z data, calculates the tilt angles using `atan2`, and logs events exceeding a threshold of 30.0 degrees to a specified log file. The program includes robust error handling for I2C communication failures, handles sensor-absent and bus-error paths, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including signal handling for Ctrl+C.

