This code sets up the HMC5883L magnetometer on a Raspberry Pi Zero W using the pigpio library. It configures the sensor and continuously reads raw data to compute hard-iron offsets. The offsets are applied to the latest raw reading every 500 ms, and the offset-corrected values are printed to stdout. The program handles I2C read/write errors and ensures clean resource release on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

