This code provides a basic framework for a smart home lighting system using the pigpio library on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It reads a schedule from a file, checks the current time against the schedule, and fades the brightness of relays using PWM. The program handles signals to cleanly shut down and release resources. Note that the code assumes the schedule file is correctly formatted and that the Raspberry Pi has the pigpio library installed.

