This code sets up a proximity-based automated door system using the VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It uses the pigpio library for I2C and GPIO control. The program performs a software reset, initializes the sensor, and continuously polls the sensor for distance data. It logs the distance to stdout and controls a relay to simulate door opening based on the distance. The program handles errors and performs a clean shutdown on SIGINT.

