This code sets up a Raspberry Pi to read data from an MPU-6050 gyroscope using SPI and libgpiod for GPIO control. It reads the gyroscope data, checks for invalid data, and blinks an LED if any axis exceeds a threshold. The data is stored in a circular buffer, and on a SIGINT signal, the buffer is printed as CSV. The program handles errors and releases resources on exit.

