This code sets up a basic fire alarm system using the libgpiod library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It monitors a flame sensor on GPIO17, activates a buzzer and an LED on GPIO18 and GPIO23 respectively when a flame is detected, and logs each detection event with a timestamp. The program includes robust error handling and resource cleanup, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful shutdown.

