This code sets up a closed-loop speed control system for two DC motors using the pigpio library on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It includes a PI controller with anti-windup clamping and handles encoder stall detection. The program compiles cleanly with `-Wall` and uses atomic operations for shared encoder counters. It also handles SIGINT to stop the motors and release resources cleanly.

